# Day File Convention

Every new day of content (Day 27, Day 28, ... Day 100) must follow this pattern exactly.

## 1. Create the day file

Write the day's content to its own file:

```
days/day27.html
days/day28.html
...
```

The file contains **only** the chapter-divider block and lesson-card blocks for that day. Nothing else.

The file must start with the chapter-divider element and end just before the next chapter would begin. Example structure:

```html
      <div class="chapter-divider reveal" id="chapter-day-27" data-chapter="day-27">
        <span class="chapter-divider__pill">Day 27</span>
        <h2 class="chapter-divider__title">Your Day Title Here</h2>
        <p class="chapter-divider__note">Short description of the day.</p>
      </div>

      <article class="lesson-card reveal" id="section-N" data-section="N" data-chapter="day-27">
        ...
      </article>
```

## 2. Add the placeholder in index.html

Inside `<main>` in `index.html`, add exactly one line at the correct position (after the previous day's placeholder):

```html
      <div data-include='days/day27.html'></div>
```

**Never add new day content inline in index.html.** The include loader fetches all `[data-include]` divs in parallel before lesson boot finishes.

## 3. What still goes in index.html

These items still belong in `index.html` directly (not in the day file):

- The sidebar TOC entry for the new day (inside `.toc-chapter` list)
- The hero stat update ("Day N of 100 published")
- The footer stat update

## 4. What still goes in styles.css

CSS chapter color rules for the new day still go in `styles.css`:

```css
.chapter-divider[data-chapter="day-27"] { border-left-color: var(--chapter-day-27); }
.lesson-card[data-chapter="day-27"] { border-top-color: var(--chapter-day-27); }
```

After any `styles.css` change, run `embed-css.sh` to sync the embedded `<style>` block in `index.html`.

## 5. Checklist before finishing a new day

- [ ] `days/dayN.html` created with chapter-divider and all lesson-card blocks
- [ ] `<div data-include='days/dayN.html'></div>` added in the correct position inside `<main>` in `index.html`
- [ ] Sidebar TOC entry added in `index.html`
- [ ] Hero and footer day count updated in `index.html`
- [ ] CSS color rules added in `styles.css`
- [ ] `embed-css.sh` run after any `styles.css` change
- [ ] No day content written inline inside `index.html`
